% This is a placeholder for the recovery power stage Simulink subsystem.
% In a real MATLAB/Simulink environment, this would be a graphical subsystem
% implementing an averaged model of the bidirectional DC-DC converter
% (buck/boost) with PID controller for active cell balancing.

% The subsystem should implement:
% - Averaged model of bidirectional DC-DC converter (buck/boost topology)
% - PID controller for regulating recovery current based on error signal
% - Interface with decision engine to receive recovery action commands
% - Modeling of power transfer between cells during balancing
%
% Inputs:
% - Recovery action command (pulse_deplating, equilibration, gas_recombination,
%   short_isolation, none, or proportional control signal)
% - Battery voltages (source and target cell voltages)
% - Current sensing feedback
% - System parameters (inductance, capacitance, switching frequency)
% - Safety limits (max current, max voltage, thermal limits)
%
% Outputs:
% - Converter duty cycle command
% - Estimated recovery current
% - Power transfer status
% - Converter efficiency estimate
% - Fault/protection indicators
%
% Bidirectional DC-DC Averaged Model:
% For buck mode (V_in > V_out):
%   V_out = D * V_in
%   I_in = D * I_out
% For boost mode (V_out > V_in):
%   V_out = V_in / (1 - D)
%   I_in = I_out / (1 - D)
% Where D is duty cycle (0 <= D <= 1)
%
% Averaged equations can be written to handle both modes smoothly
%
% PID Controller:
%   u(t) = Kp * e(t) + Ki * ∫e(t)dt + Kd * de(t)/dt
% Where e(t) = reference_current - measured_current
% Gains Kp, Ki, Kd tuned for stable recovery control
%
% Recovery Actions (matching decision engine):
% - pulse_deplating: Apply depolishing pulses
% - equilibration: Equalize cell voltages
% - gas_recombination: Recombine generated gases
% - short_isolation: Isolate shorted cell
% - none: No recovery action
% - Proportional: Variable strength based on control signal
%
% This file represents the intended structure. Actual implementation requires
% using MATLAB Simulink editor to create the graphical subsystem with:
% - Averaged model blocks for inductor, capacitor, and semiconductor losses
% - PID controller block (or PID gains in Sum/Gain/Integrator blocks)
% - Switching logic or PWM generator for duty cycle
% - Math operations for voltage/current calculations
% - Lookup tables or logic for recovery action mapping
% - Safety limit blocks (saturation, comparison)
% - Output ports for control signals and monitoring